{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>וראיתם</b> in gematria: ציצית ביום." "<b>וזכרתם</b> — ketiv: remembrance through tzitzit. Therefore He commanded to make four tzitzit on the four corners of his garment, so that wherever he turns he will remember. And in each, five knots, so that he will remember the five books of the Torah. And there are in each eight strings, so that he will refrain from transgression with the eight limbs that habituate a person to transgression, and they are: ears, eyes, mouth, nose, hands, feet, the genitals, and the heart. And if he guarded himself from transgression, he merits to ascend above the eight heavens, as it is written: 'And the soul of my lord shall be bound in the bundle of life.' And if he transgressed with them, he is punished with eight punishments: beating of the grave and the seven chambers of Gehinnom." "<b>ציצית</b> = 600. And eight strings and five knots = 613, to tell you that the commandment of tzitzit is weighed against the entire Torah. 'At all times your garments shall be white' — in gematria: זה ציצית לבגדיכם." "<b>כל מצות ה'</b> = 612. 'I' and 'You shall have no' — from the mouth of the Almighty they heard them."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :register {:flags {3 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:20.327860732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}